{
  "sourceLanguage" : "zh-Hans",
  "strings" : {
    "「值物」取「物有所值、物尽其用」之意，又谐音「植物」，呼应那只小胡萝卜吉祥物。这只胡萝卜也是向五月天阿信的「卜卜」致敬——我们做了去真人化的原创设计。买之前想清楚，买之后好好用，就是对每件物品最大的尊重。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "\"Zhizu\" (值物) means \"worth its value\" and \"making the most of things,\" and sounds like the Chinese word for \"plant\" — a nod to our little carrot mascot. The carrot is also a tribute to Mayday Ashin's \"Bubu,\" reimagined as an original, non-literal design. Think before you buy, and use it well afterward — that's the greatest respect for everything you own."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "「日均」是怎么算的？" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How is \"daily cost\" calculated?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
